## If I Were Building This As A Template

My section order would be:

```text
Navbar
↓
Hero
↓
About Company
↓
Products
↓
Why Choose Us
↓
Industries Served
↓
Process
↓
Testimonials
↓
Certifications
↓
Contact Form
↓
Footer
```

Notice what's *not* there:

```text
Fancy animations
Complex page transitions
Glassmorphism everywhere
```

Food distribution businesses usually care more about:

```text
Trust
Reliability
Quality
Supply Capacity
```

than cutting-edge design trends.

If you build a meat distributor template, I'd lean into **clean, trustworthy, industrial-professional design** rather than the cinematic style you used for your portfolio. That difference in visual language is what makes templates feel tailored to their industries.
